<title>UK: Lonrho yr pretax profit up 12.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Lonrho yr pretax profit up 12.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>				 (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.9p		  vs 8.9</p>
<p> Final dividend (pence) 3.0		    vs 3.0</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 5.25		   vs 5.25</p>
<p> Pretax		     170		    vs 151</p>
<p> Turnover		   2,070		  vs 2.043</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts had forecast pre-tax profits in a range between 156 and 166 million stg. Turnover figure is before exceptional items. Lonrho said it was still committed to separating its mining and trading businesses. It gave no further details. It said talks to dispose of its Princess hotel chain were progressing.</p>
<p>South Africa's Anglo American Corp is Lonrho's largest single shareholder with a 28 percent stake.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
